# be-host headless as `:dev` runs it, driven by the same commands as `drive`
# and painted with every app's own paint (guides/testing_a_gui.md, Testing
# editors together). The host is built for a worker, so the tests run on Linux
# x86_64 only. Each test is an action of its own under ./scripts/verify
# (run_apart in buck/cargo/defs.bzl), against a host that stages only the
# apps it names here beside the ones every host needs (apps.bzl), so it
# builds and reruns only for those. A test not named here stages every app:
# keep it so for a test whose paintings show every block type, such as the add
# menu's.
